WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.659
Hybrid and cluster AI telemetry starts with understanding the full path from user request to model,

00:00:06.659 --> 00:00:08.708
data, infrastructure, policy, and response.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:14.037
A production AI workflow may cross many systems before it returns an answer.

00:00:14.037 --> 00:00:20.596
Telemetry should make that path visible enough that teams can connect user experience to model behavior,

00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:23.465
data freshness, resource pressure, and operational controls.

00:00:23.465 --> 00:00:25.515
Use multiple signal types together.

00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:27.974
Metrics show trends and alertable conditions.

00:00:27.974 --> 00:00:29.614
Logs explain discrete events.

00:00:29.614 --> 00:00:31.253
Traces connect distributed work.

00:00:31.253 --> 00:00:34.942
Events and audit records capture important changes and decisions.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:36.992
Health checks, profiles, resource telemetry,

00:00:36.992 --> 00:00:39.861
and pipeline signals complete the operating picture.

00:00:39.861 --> 00:00:44.370
The best telemetry design chooses signals because they answer real questions,

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:47.240
not because a platform can emit them.

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.699
Specialized AI infrastructure needs special attention.

00:00:49.699 --> 00:00:53.798
GPUs, accelerators, storage, queues, vector stores, retrieval indexes, model gateways,

00:00:53.798 --> 00:00:56.668
and batch pipelines can all influence reliability.

00:00:56.668 --> 00:01:01.177
Monitor them with enough context to separate capacity, placement, data, retrieval,

00:01:01.177 --> 00:01:02.407
and model-serving issues.

00:01:02.407 --> 00:01:07.325
At the same time, protect sensitive data through privacy-aware logging, data minimization,

00:01:07.325 --> 00:01:09.375
and governed access to telemetry.

00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:11.835
Finally, make telemetry usable during pressure.

00:01:11.835 --> 00:01:15.934
Consistent labels, request IDs, trace IDs, model versions, cluster names,

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:20.443
and deployment versions connect scattered signals into a path of investigation.

00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:24.952
Alerts, SLOs, runbooks, and post-incident reviews turn telemetry into operational readiness.

00:01:24.952 --> 00:01:28.231
Good AI telemetry is not just more data.

00:01:28.231 --> 00:01:32.740
It is disciplined evidence that helps teams act responsibly and quickly.
